  "prefLabel": "Alc 102.03 Licensed alcohol and drug counselor (LADC)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Alc 102.03 “Licensed alcohol and drug counselor (LADC)” means “licensed alcohol and drug counselor” as defined in RSA 330-C:2, XIII, namely “an individual licensed by the office of professional licensure and certification to practice substance use counseling who meets the qualifications set forth in this chapter.”\n\nSource. #8169, eff 9-21-04; ss by 9417, eff 3-14-09 (from Alc 102.02); ss by #14585, eff 6-1-26",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/alc100-500.html"
